  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Venture Capital Association set up EAVCA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a growing number of active providers of long-term risk capital to Small and Medium-sized businesses in Uganda, there is a need to further collaborate, promote finance to SMEs and have a representative body for the SME PE (private equity) and VC (venture capital) sector. This project aims to set up a local Ugandan Chapter of the existing East Africa Venture Capital Association (EAVCA). EAVCA is an umbrella organisation that represents PE and VC funds in East Africa. The local Ugandan Chapter will collaborate with the central EAVCA based in Nairobi but will have its activities, members and resources. This project aims to help small and medium-sized businesses in Uganda get the funding they need for growth.</narrative>
  </description>
